{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"Thus did the children of Israel do all the work\"</b> — all the labor of the Tabernacle. And He calls it \"work\" (עֲבֹדָה) to say that they made it for the service of the honored Name, in the manner of \"and you shall serve YHWH your Elohim\" (Exodus 23:25), \"and Him shall you serve\" (Deuteronomy 13:5). And it is also possible that here \"all the work\" refers to the utensils, in the same usage as where it says (Exodus 39:40) \"all the utensils of the service of the Tabernacle.\" And it mentioned the utensils first, to say that even with the utensils they were meticulous and made them as commanded; and afterward it mentioned \"and Moses saw all the labor\"."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "The opening word וְטַעַם ('and the reason') introduces Ramban's explanation of the verse's wording; rendered as 'The reason for' to preserve his exegetical framing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:23:06.152900293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}